label IT DOESN'T MATTER
\doctor: I just need to know if you're okay. How are you feeling?
alien (sonho/triste e boca aberta): I feel dizzy.
alien: Since I came  back to my body after speaking to you, it’s as if my mind has been shaken in a way that I never felt before.
alien: Usually, when I’m back inside my body, I feel all the pains that they gave me.
alien (sonho/triste e boca fecada): But this time, I only felt a deep emptiness.
alien: As if my body was sucked from me, and flung far away.
alien (sonho/triste e boca aberta): And I can still hear their voices all around me, screaming in pain.
alien: And I could hear HER voice…
alien: She-[pause] she said she loved me…
alien: They had to pay, doctor. It was the only thing in my mind
alien (sonho/triste e boca fecada): ...
alien: When I came back to myself, you were talking to me.[br]For a moment, I felt peace.
alien: But then everything came back again, and I had to come up here.
alien: This place helped me survive.
\doctor: L3XA. I’m sorry.
\doctor: I shouldn’t have left you alone with them.
\doctor: I shouldn’t have left you alone with them.
\doctor: I should have protected you.
alien: I’m scared, doctor. I don’t know how much I can take.
\doctor: I’m going to protect you. I’m going to wake up right now and go to the lab and-
alien (sonho/triste e boca aberta): Please, stay here with me.
\doctor: But–
alien: I need you.
L3XA pulls me towards them, embracing me. My body feels their warmth in the midst of this cold, empty space.
I need them too, at this moment.
I want to be with them forever…
